5-bae6-8b48a3343a8c","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 1942 (commit 39e2ea3b52, branch b0a5-lifecycle-collisions off origin/main e278425d7a).\n\nMECHANISM CONFIRMED IN CODE (not taken on faith): scripts/gen_config_reference.py::_lifecycle_index had TWO index.setdefault(replacement, ...) calls — one over _cfg_deprecations(), one over _cfg_tombstones(). First-wins, so a second alias/tombstone aimed at the same canonical replacement key was silently discarded. Sole consumer is _schema_rows() -> the Lifecycle table cell.\n\nNO LIVE COLLISION today, verified by enumerating the registry: cfg deprecations = [verify.overlap_enabled -> verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets]; cfg tombstones = [verify.require_verdict_for_close -> verify.require_completion_verification_for_close] plus six with empty replacement. Collision count = 0. Defensive fix, as the plan says.\n\nRED FIRST: both new guards were run against the UNMODIFIED generator and failed for the right reason — the first note rendered and the second was absent, e.g.\n  AssertionError: second alias note dropped from 'code_health.include_extensions' row: | `code_health.include_extensions` | `list[str]` | `[]` | active — supersedes alias `legacy.first_alias` (permanent alias) |\nThat is the drop itself, not an unrelated error. After the fix: 14 passed.\n\nGENERATED DOCS: none needed regenerating. The single-note case renders byte-identically ('active — ' + the one note), so python scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check exits 0 against the committed tree and git status shows no doc modification. docs/env-vars.md is also unaffected — its generator scans DEFAULT_SCAN_ROOT = src/rebar only, and python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check exits 0.\n\nGATES: make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS (576 files); python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check run DIRECTLY -> 'active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0' exit 0. .github/complexity-baseline.json untouched.","timestamp":1787196015808218001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI on patch set 1 of Gerrit 1942: 1 failed, 14508 passed. The single failure is tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin_and_keeps_refs_isolated — a shutil.copytree race against git auto-maintenance's objects/maintenance.lock, with no path to the config-reference generator this change touches.\n\nPer scope discipline it was NOT absorbed into this change. Filed as bug regardable-superduper-whiteeye (dca1-f641-caeb-4df4), linked discovered_from this ticket, with the mechanism, the deterministic reproduction, and a remove-the-race fix specified. Same root-cause class as the already-closed chewed-illicit-blacklemur / icicled-unstable-urial. A reasoned 'recheck' citing that ticket was posted on 1942.\n\nLocal validation of the blast radius (all green): tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py, test_gen_env_registry.py, test_generated_surface_markers.py, test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py, test_ci_workflow_parity.py, test_gerrit_docs_only.py, test_llm_config_pointer.py, and tests/scripts — 1133 passed, 2 skipped.","timestamp":1787198229656767001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"LANDED. Gerrit 1942 reached LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 with 0 unresolved comments after the reasoned recheck, and was submitted (Rebase-If-Necessary) as origin/main commit 21f90dfac282662c679ebdd52e90df2acf0608e2.\n\nVerified on merged main: scripts/gen_config_reference.py::_lifecycle_index now accumulates into notes.setdefault(replacement, []).append(...) for both the deprecation and tombstone loops and returns {key: 'active — ' + '; '.join(parts)}.\n\nLocal validation before push (all with the worktree venv first on PATH):\n- make lint PASS\n- make typecheck PASS (576 source files)\n- python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check run directly: active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0\n- python scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check exit 0 (no doc regeneration needed)\n- python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check exit 0 (docs/env-vars.md unaffected)\n- tests/interfaces: 1936 passed, 9 skipped (the test that flaked in CI passes locally, confirming a race)\n- blast-radius unit + scripts tests: 1133 passed, 2 skipped\nCI on the green run: full suite passed.\n\nFollow-up filed, not absorbed: regardable-superduper-whiteeye (dca1-f641-caeb-4df4).","timestamp":1787200002450601001}],"created_at":1787158929772021001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"aca630c2-c882-4ad3-b786-c361c03d4408","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3199-d739-8804-4746"},{"link_uuid":"892caf67-1b8c-4436-8518-95b68a3bf301","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a880-b7e0-4b67-4196"}],"description":"Latent robustness gap found by the LLM code review of Gerrit 1905 (C4).\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`scripts/gen_config_reference.py::_lifecycle_index()` uses `dict.setdefault` when mapping a\ncanonical schema key to its lifecycle note, so if one canonical replacement key is ever the\ntarget of MORE THAN ONE cfg deprecation alias and/or tombstone, only the first-encountered\nnote survives and the rest are silently dropped from the generated `docs/config-reference.md`.\nConfirmed in code: both loops in `_lifecycle_index` call `index.setdefault(replacement, ...)`.\n\nNo collision exists today (each cfg replacement key is targeted exactly once across\n`rebar._deprecations.REGISTRY` + `tombstones()`), so current generated output is correct.\nThis is a defensive fix that stops a future deprecation from silently deleting doc content.\n\n## Approach\n\nAccumulate the notes per canonical key instead of `setdefault`: collect them into a list keyed\nby replacement, then join them into the single `Lifecycle` table cell. The single-note case\nmust render byte-identically to today so `docs/config-reference.md` needs no regeneration and\nthe committed-tree drift oracle stays green.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` — rewrite `_lifecycle_index` to accumulate.\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py` — add the held-out collision guards.\n\nNo other module reads `_lifecycle_index`; `docs/env-vars.md` is out of scope because its\ngenerator only scans `src/rebar`.\n\n## Testing\n\nHeld-out guards seed collisions by monkeypatching the generator's `_cfg_deprecations` /\n`_cfg_tombstones` accessors onto a real schema key, then assert both notes survive into that\nkey's rendered table row:\n\n- Two deprecated aliases sharing one replacement — both alias names appear in the row.\n- One deprecated alias plus one tombstone sharing one replacement — both notes appear.\n- Each guard is confirmed RED against unmodified `main` (the second note is absent) before\n  the fix lands.\n- Regression: the whole existing oracle, including the read-only committed-tree `--check`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `_lifecycle_index` accumulates every lifecycle note for a canonical key with no silent\n  drop; checked by `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py -q` passing the\n  new collision guards.\n- [x] A test seeds a 2-alias collision and asserts both notes appear in that key's\n  `config-reference.md` row; checked by the same pytest run, and by observing it FAIL on\n  unmodified `main` first.\n- [x] `python scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check` exits 0 against the committed tree and\n  the pre-existing oracle stays green; checked by that command plus the full\n  `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py` run.\n- [x] Gates stay green; checked by `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and\n  `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reporting new=0 increased=0 stale=0.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/gen_config_reference.py","reason":"accumulate lifecycle notes per canonical key instead of setdefault"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py","reason":"held-out multi-alias canonical-key collision guards"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","a880-b7e0-4b67-4196"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"15e235c1-af46-420a-90be-4b41337388f7","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b0a5-f5c0-e516-4fdc","ticket_type":"task","title":"Harden gen_config_reference _lifecycle_index against multi-alias canonical-key collisions","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2ac326fc-a4ad-4628-a3a8-8ac03b0ba6e5","10ae8332-e38f-4dd7-84dd-fe44f5daea1e","b6af9f33-f483-4dac-8774-45ad9b53c742","11c2127c-ab42-498d-b735-bf72e5123473","e867d010-60db-48ac-be3e-95c87b16a61d","793065ad-7f7b-43fa-842b-a1deb9c5ec13","892caf67-1b8c-4436-8518-95b68a3bf301","e143e561-1794-439e-9245-29d02947411e","bd347435-fb7c-4ed2-88dc-abdc65c707bb","8fd6fd1d-0fe3-43cc-b46a-921cbcc17b4c","15e235c1-af46-420a-90be-4b41337388f7","e362ee81-78c2-4d27-a418-6027fd93e14a"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787206037155012802,"uuid":"b3516cda-ff4e-45ca-a5ab-59fea0519590"}